WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.570
Hi, welcome back to
Nagarjuna, course number three.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:10.020
And we're going to start a new
chapter now, it's chapter 10.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.483
And it has a great name,
and we'll see the name here.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.171
It's called,

00:00:17.171 --> 00:00:21.130
ME DANG BUD SHING BRTAG PA

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.140
an examination or an investigation

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.310
into fire and firewood.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.510
And we're still getting this argument.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.380
You see, there's still this argument that

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.830
until the young lady with the telescope

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.020
looks at the stars, we cannot
call her an astronomer.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.890
So looking at the stars must happen

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.990
before she comes out of her house,

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.950
before the astronomer
comes out of her house.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.560
It has to, all right?

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.890
So there's some confusion there.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.477
And the other guy says,

00:00:54.477 --> 00:00:59.009
"Listen, I've got a
solution, let's talk about

00:00:59.009 --> 00:00:59.950
ME DANG BUD SHING

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.850
"let's talk about fire and firewood.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.157
"Let's talk about fire and firewood.

00:01:06.157 --> 00:01:08.870
"And according to me, that's
going to clarify everything.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.770
"We will solve these problems.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.420
If we just look at the
example of fire and firewood."

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.120
And mainly those guys like
the lower Abhidharma guys

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.530
who want to say that
the eye was there first

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.040
and then there was a scene.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.570
The astronomer was wandering around,

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.050
and then they looked at a star,

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.480
and they were called an astronomer

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.270
even before they looked
to the stars, right?

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.910
That's their idea.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.870
They say, "Our position is supported

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.540
by the example of fire and firewood",

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.590
the relationship between
fire and firewood.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.903
Now to really appreciate this chapter,

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.300
I'd like to explore with you first.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.110
Let's do our "getting to
know Sanskrit" assignment,

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.470
and let's look at four Sanskrit words

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.493
that are going to help us
understand this chapter.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.315
The first word is "indhana", say indhana.

00:02:06.315 --> 00:02:07.160
- [Audience] Indhana.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.797
- Okay, the Tibetan is BUD SHING,

00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:13.580
and this indhana comes from a root,

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.310
and you see that square
root symbol √id or √ind,

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.200
which means "to kindle" or "to set fire",

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.790
to set fire to something.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.240
And I think it's related
to the Indo-European,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.510
which is kind of an older
root system called √ed,

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.970
which means "to eat", and
sometimes n's drop out,

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:38.600
like √ind becomes √ed in
Indo-European, and it means to eat.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.570
And some cognates or some English examples

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:45.860
are: edible, and eat, and obese.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.130
And they all have the same root √ed,

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.260
which is related to the Sanskrit root √id,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.920
which means "to burn".

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.550
The kindle part, which
means to burn something,

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:02.550
is related... I think it is
the precursor of a root √kand,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.680
which means to burn.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:11.680
And you see √kand in
incandescent, candle, kindle.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.180
And I think there was an ancient S before,

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.720
which is √scand or
"schund" (pronunciation),

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.230
and that came into the word shine.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.288
So all of these words for burning:

00:03:23.288 --> 00:03:26.654
id, ind, ed, kand, and scand,

00:03:27.563 --> 00:03:30.690
are all related to burning, scand,

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.570
all related to burning.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:37.570
Now we were talking about
the eye looking at something,

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.290
at an object.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.870
So Michael's eye looks at the juice.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.780
Michael's eyes looks at the orange juice,

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.000
the orange colored juice,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.690
and you have three distinct things.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.690
You have the doer,
which Chоney Lama calls,

00:03:57.394 --> 00:03:59.240
NYE BAR LEN PA PO

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.157
the agent, let's say,

00:04:01.157 --> 00:04:04.023
the one who undertakes the action.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.840
And then you have the
object of the action,

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.172
which is called

00:04:08.172 --> 00:04:10.450
NYE BAR LEN PA BYA, NYE BAR LEN BYA

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.906
and then you have the
action itself, which is,

00:04:13.906 --> 00:04:15.547
NYE BAR LEN PA

00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:19.670
NYE BAR LEN PA PO, NYE BAR
LEN BYA and NYE BAR LEN PA

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.170
meaning the object of the action,

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.200
the agent of the action and the action,

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.340
which is seeing in this case.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:30.513
Now I challenge you,
in the case of a fire,

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.450
who is the agent and who is the action?

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.270
Who is the object of the agent?

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.397
Who is the agent in the case of a fire?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.100
And I'll give you some choices here.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.110
Here's the first choice:

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.090
indhana, the wood.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.430
Is the wood the agent?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.430
Is the wood, like the eye,
which does/sees the object

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.753
because the wood feeds the fire.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.600
There's a possibility.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.080
Or, let's go onto the
next Sanskrit word here,

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.123
which is "agni".

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.860
And as you guys probably
know, agni means "fire"

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.810
and what's interesting is it comes

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.440
from a verbal root √ag,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.260
which means to move
like a snake, like this.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:25.260
So the flames are movers, agni.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.490
They're dancing, dancing.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.780
Agni means dancing. Agni means fire.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.840
And in the Indo-European,

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.863
again you have these words for driving,

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.540
moving related to √ag that we had before.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.973
And then you have the cognates:

00:05:39.973 --> 00:05:42.950
act, active, agile, and agent,

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.460
all coming from the same root as √ag,

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.490
to move and get things done.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.250
And then there's a suffix -ni,

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.340
which makes nouns out of verbs.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.410
So agni means fire.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.330
And in English, you
get the words "ignite",

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.480
and "igneous", meaning made from fire,

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.153
stone made from fire.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.010
So that's the fire.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:10.010
Now again, so, so far we have
firewood and we have fire.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.620
Is it that the fire acts on the firewood

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.050
or is it that the
firewood creates the fire?

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.440
Which is the agent?

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.940
With the eye it's easy,
the eye sees the bottle.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.650
The bottle is the object,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.560
the seeing is the verb,
and the eye is the subject.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:33.110
But in the case of a fire, who
is the doer and what is done?

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:38.110
Is the fire the result of the wood,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.490
or is it that the fire acts on the wood?

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.790
Is the wood the object of the fire,

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:48.020
or is the wood the agent of the fire?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.220
You've got to think about it.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.690
It's confusing, to me it's confusing.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.840
Okay, let's do a couple more words.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.690
And then we'll get to the real class.

00:06:56.632 --> 00:06:59.045
Dāha, say dāha.

00:06:59.045 --> 00:06:59.878
- [Audience] Dāha.

00:06:59.878 --> 00:07:02.990
- Okay, and that means
SREG PA, it means burning.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.910
The burning.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:08.443
So the fire burns the
wood. Can we say that?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.763
Or the wood feeds the fire?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:19.000
But anyway, √dah is the root
here, which means to burn.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.567
I think it's related to "daha",

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.540
and then "dh" is sometimes
changed into the F in English,

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:30.030
which is F, and then to make it an agent,

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.913
you have to call it a "fa-er",
and then I think fire.

00:07:34.923 --> 00:07:39.923
And a parallel case is where
√dhr, which became dharma,

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.030
which means to hold something,

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.420
it comes into the word "firm".

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.290
And it's also the root
for the word "tree",

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:53.780
because trees were the
most immovable thing

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.270
in the ancient world.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.110
You couldn't move a tree.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:08:01.113
So there you go, √dhr and √dah.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:03.568
One more word for you guys:

00:08:03.568 --> 00:08:06.601
in this chapter, they're
going to talk about

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:09.190
fire burning wood

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:12.890
until the wood is used
up and then the fire,

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:17.040
here's the next word, nirvana.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.830
Isn't that interesting?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.660
So you always hear about nirvana,

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:25.600
meaning "to blow out" [blows] a candle,

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.210
but here in Nagarjuna, in this chapter,

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:33.210
he's using it without
reference to liberation.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:37.640
It just means the fire went out, nirvana.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.183
It blew itself out.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.160
It burned itself out. The
fire burned itself out.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.275
So nirvana. And by the
way the V in Sanskrit

00:08:47.275 --> 00:08:50.003
is more of... almost like a W (nirwana).

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:51.958
The Tibetan is,

00:08:51.958 --> 00:08:52.791
MYANG NGAN LAS 'DAS PA

00:08:52.791 --> 00:08:56.023
which is a meaning translation
and not literal translation,

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.760
which means to go beyond grief.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.680
And here's the parts of the word nirvana,

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.560
which I want you to learn.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.623
Nis- is a prefix, which means "not".

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.750
And it means "out and down",

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.403
meaning something
degenerates until it's gone.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.190
And then you have the
words nether, beneath,

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.070
and underneath

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.020
comes from this.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.930
√van means to blow.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.360
That's an easy one for English cognates:

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:28.270
you have fan, vent and wind.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:31.010
So blow out [blows] is nirvana.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:35.430
I think it's exciting in this chapter

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:38.140
that we see nirvana used

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:42.000
only as a fire being blown out.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.160
And that gives you a nice insight

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:49.160
into the idea of blowing out
your anger at your husband,

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.730
because you realize it's coming from you.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.730
That's nirvana.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.610
All right, let's go back to the beginning

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:01.320
of this chapter ten.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.180
And we're going to go through
the verses one by one.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.620
Now the first verse is
traditionally split into two.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:12.390
The first verse is traditionally treated

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.703
first two Tibetan lines, and
then second two Tibetan lines.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:23.890
And by the way, the Sanskrit still exists,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.440
which is exciting. If you
want to learn Sanskrit,

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:30.870
this book is a great text
to learn Sanskrit from.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.110
I don't emphasize learning Sanskrit

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.240
because most of the Sanskrit is gone.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.116
So whereas in Tibetan

00:10:39.116 --> 00:10:43.699
you have maybe 500,000 important books.

00:10:43.699 --> 00:10:47.970
In Sanskrit you have a few hundred, maybe.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:50.630
So, I don't know if it's worth the effort

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:53.383
to spend six, seven
years learning Sanskrit.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.570
The Tibetan is exactly
the same as the Sanskrit.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:04.180
I rarely, rarely, rarely
see any difference.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.380
All right, here we go.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.353
First half of the first verse.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.781
,BUD SHING GANG DE ME YIN NA,

00:11:14.781 --> 00:11:17.631
,BYED PA PO DANG LAS GCIG 'GYUR,

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:22.110
Now the first... the way that Nagarjuna

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.340
explores the other guy's example,

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.190
The other guy says,

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:30.027
"Look, you can understand all
your questions, Nagarjuna,

00:11:30.027 --> 00:11:33.643
"if you just use the example
of a fire and the firewood,

00:11:33.643 --> 00:11:36.597
"and the interaction of
the fire and the firewood,

00:11:36.597 --> 00:11:37.947
"you're getting all complicated,

00:11:37.947 --> 00:11:39.710
"you don't have to do it."

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:44.470
If you just think about how
a fire consumes firewood,

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.100
then everything's clear.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.950
The discussion of whether the little girl

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.890
had to be there first,

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.870
or that looking at the
stars had to be there first,

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:56.730
and then the little girl
was an astronomer later,

00:11:56.730 --> 00:12:01.430
the whole discussion is
decided by fire and firewood.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.150
Just stick to fire and firewood.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.407
And Nagarjuna says, "Not really."

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:07.870
He's like, "I don't think so."

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:10.370
- Well, what's wrong with that, Nagarjuna?

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:14.193
- Well, is the fire separate
from the firewood or not?

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.250
Is the fire a separate
thing than the firewood?

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.350
What do you guys think?

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.027
I mean, okay, listen, Nagarjuna says,

00:12:23.027 --> 00:12:26.110
"Listen, either the firewood is the fire

00:12:27.427 --> 00:12:29.767
"or the firewood is not
the fire. Which one?"

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:35.047
And he says, "Okay, let's say

00:12:35.047 --> 00:12:37.360
"you say they are the same
thing. Well, they're not."

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.160
I mean, you can't burn
yourself on the firewood

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.770
if it's not.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:46.680
So let's eliminate one
possibility from the beginning.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:51.080
We can say that the
firewood is not the fire.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.480
They're not the same thing.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:53.603
So here it says,

00:12:53.603 --> 00:12:55.620
BUD SHING GANG DE ME YIN NA

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.493
if the firewood were the fire,

00:12:58.493 --> 00:13:00.600
BYED PA PO DANG LAS GCIG 'GYUR

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:05.600
then the agent, then the
burner and the burning

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.667
would be the same thing.

00:13:07.667 --> 00:13:11.080
The burning would be the burner.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:14.760
If you take the wood to
be the cause of the fire,

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.670
then the wood would be the burning.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.080
Then the wood would be the burning.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:22.000
It's not possible that the fire

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.930
and the wood are the same thing.

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:26.640
So let's eliminate that possibility.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:29.240
Let's go on to the
possibility that the fire

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:33.050
and the wood are not the same thing,

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:33.980
and that they're separate.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:37.823
Okay, we go to the second
half of the first...

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:44.537
Oh and by the way, that picture,
we missed a picture here,

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.530
I was supposed to explain a picture here:

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.520
people looking at a campfire.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.670
And I don't know, where
I grew up in Arizona,

00:13:54.670 --> 00:13:57.110
it's very popular to go out in the desert

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:00.410
and make a small fire. Small
fire, not this big one.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.590
And you sit around the campfire

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:04.810
and you look at the fire.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.527
So the guy says, the other guy says,

00:14:08.527 --> 00:14:13.527
"Look, what the eye does
when it looks at a star

00:14:14.497 --> 00:14:17.360
"is not unreal. It's real."

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:19.750
Meaning for him it's self-existent.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:22.100
It comes from its own side. Why?

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:24.850
Because the- fire and
what it burns are real.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:29.537
So he says, "When
somebody looks at a star,

00:14:29.537 --> 00:14:31.387
"it's really happening

00:14:31.387 --> 00:14:33.757
"because it's really happening

00:14:33.757 --> 00:14:36.508
"when fire burns wood same thing."

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:37.577
RIGS PA MGO MTSUNGS

00:14:37.577 --> 00:14:39.563
means parallel reasoning.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.910
Okay, next verse, second part of...

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.363
Oh, by the way, one more
picture before the...

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:57.193
Nagarjuna says, "If the fire was the wood,

00:14:58.257 --> 00:15:02.147
"then the person making a pot out of clay

00:15:02.147 --> 00:15:03.550
"would be the pot."

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.840
All right?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.300
And that's easy to understand.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.260
It's one of the few easy
things to understand

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.120
in Nagarjuna.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:13.820
That's clear: if the fire was a firewood,

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:17.590
then this girl would be a pot.

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:20.533
Then what makes the
thing would be the thing.

00:15:21.891 --> 00:15:24.490
If the fire is the wood that it burns,

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.000
then the potter is the pot that it makes.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.720
And this girl would be a pot.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.900
And this girl would be
in this girl's own hands

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.424
or something like that.

00:15:32.424 --> 00:15:34.010
Not possible.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.450
Let's go to the second half

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.266
of the first verse.

00:15:41.724 --> 00:15:46.716
anyaś ced indhanād agnir
indhanād apy ṛte bhavet

00:15:48.141 --> 00:15:51.260
,GAL TE SHING LAS ME GZHAN NA,

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.080
If the wood is not the fire,

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.970
if the wood and the fire are separate,

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.603
Now you've got to think of...

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.734
Here's a principle when
you're reading Nagarjuna.

00:16:01.734 --> 00:16:04.403
Is the fire separate from the wood or not?

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:07.820
Yeah, it's separate from the wood.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.593
Is it self-existently
separate from the wood?

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.430
You see, now, because Nagarjuna

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.890
is going to keep pulling out this word,

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:19.090
self-existently, without an observer,

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.300
with karmic seeds in their mind,

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.829
is the wood separate from the fire?

00:16:23.829 --> 00:16:24.697
And Nagarjuna says,

00:16:24.697 --> 00:16:29.229
"No, they're not separate
from their own side."

00:16:29.229 --> 00:16:30.512
So you have to remember that.

00:16:30.512 --> 00:16:34.227
GAL TE SHING LAS ME GZHAN NA

00:16:34.227 --> 00:16:38.910
If the wood was distinct from the fire,

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:42.000
then they would not overlap.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.860
They would never make contact.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.344
When I say overlap, I mean make contact.

00:16:46.344 --> 00:16:48.610
- Geshe-la, it is not the same thing.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.730
To touch something and
to overlap is different.

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:55.590
- Look, here's contact
and here's overlapping.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:58.770
But you've got to understand
that if they make contact,

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:01.050
some part has to overlap.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.320
Some part has to overlap. Why?

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.110
There has to be a point of contact.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:10.110
In mathematics, a point is a single spot

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.560
that has no width and no length.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.000
But in reality, if something touches,

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.690
there has to be a point of contact.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:23.490
There has to be so many
millimeters of place

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.420
where they overlap,

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.790
where they occupied the same spot,

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.620
or you couldn't have contact.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.460
There can't be contact.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:37.460
So he says, "If the fire and
the wood never make contact,"

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.680
meaning they are separate,

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.640
if they are different from each other,

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.620
if they never made contact,

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.590
well, then you're going
to have fires popping out

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:49.450
all over the place where there's no wood.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:50.283
- Oh, keep away, there's
a fire right there!"

00:17:50.283 --> 00:17:51.770
- What? There's no wood.

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:52.830
- Yeah, you don't need wood.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:53.663
- Why?

00:17:53.663 --> 00:17:54.496
- It's separate.

00:17:54.496 --> 00:17:56.750
They don't have to touch.

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:58.350
There doesn't have to be wood in the room

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:00.290
for a fire to break out.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.550
- Why?

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:03.830
Because all fires happen.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.720
- What do you mean all fires happen?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:08.930
- Fires happen where there's wood, right?

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.050
- Yeah.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.190
- So they touch, right?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.200
- No, they can't touch.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.033
- Why not?

00:18:13.033 --> 00:18:13.866
- They can't overlap.

00:18:13.866 --> 00:18:15.930
- Okay, so they're separate,
what's the problem with that?

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.570
- Well, then you can
have a fire in this room

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.197
if you had firewood in the next room.

00:18:20.197 --> 00:18:22.490
Because they don't have to touch.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:23.673
If they don't have to overlap

00:18:23.673 --> 00:18:25.170
then the fire could be anywhere

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:26.700
and the wood could be anywhere.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.340
Then you'd have fires breaking
out all over the place.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.580
- No, no, no, they have to touch.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.650
- Okay, if they have to touch
they have to make contact.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.810
- Yeah, then they have to overlap.

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:34.643
- Right.

00:18:34.643 --> 00:18:36.230
- Then the fire is the wood.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.830
- No. - Look, you can't have it both ways.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.620
Nagarjuna is like pulling his hair out.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:41.970
That's what happened to me.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:46.570
If they make contact,

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:50.180
then some tiny part of the
fire has to be the firewood.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.660
- No, I don't want that.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.760
- Okay, so they never make contact.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:54.640
- Right.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:56.380
- Okay, so then watch out,

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.330
you've got to have a fire
extinguisher in your toilet,

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.280
for your toilet,

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:03.600
because the fire might
pop out in the toilet.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.110
- No there's water there, Geshe-la.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:08.030
- I don't care, a fire
can happen anywhere,

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:10.570
it doesn't have to touch a wood.

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.620
If you're not confused yet,

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:17.100
I didn't do my job. Next verse.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:21.383
And he combines verse two and verse three.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:23.885
Who is he? Choney Lama.

00:19:26.735 --> 00:19:28.877
,RTAG TU 'BAR BA NYID DU 'GYUR,

00:19:28.877 --> 00:19:30.769
,'BAR BYED RGYU LAS MI 'BYUNG ZHING,

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:32.610
,RTZOM PA DON MED NYID DU 'GYUR,

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:34.485
,DE LTA YIN NA LAS KYANG MED,

00:19:34.485 --> 00:19:36.600
Okay, RTAG TU 'BAR BA NYID DU 'GYUR

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:41.543
Not only would fires break
out inside your toilet,

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.640
they would also burn forever. Why?

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.250
Because they don't burn from the wood.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.680
They just burn from themselves,

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.060
because the wood never touches the fire.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.300
- No, the fire does touch the wood.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:56.850
- Okay, then they overlap, right?

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.780
And the wood is the fire and
the fire is the wood, right?

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.130
At some point.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.200
- No, no they're separate.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.070
- Okay, then watch out,

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.760
when you take a poop causes you a fire,

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.867
the water might catch on fire.

00:20:07.867 --> 00:20:09.330
[Geshe Michael chuckles]

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:10.580
- Well, I didn't say that.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.643
- Yeah, you did. You said

00:20:11.643 --> 00:20:13.560
a fire could happen without firewood.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:14.640
- I didn't say that.

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.473
- Yeah, you did,

00:20:15.473 --> 00:20:17.350
you said it didn't have
to touch the firewood.

00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:18.690
- Yeah, I did say that.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.850
- Okay, so the fire can
be in the other room,

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:21.860
the fire can be in the toilet.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:23.840
Be careful when you take a poop.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:27.943
Okay. Something else is
going on, something's fishy.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.900
What's going on?

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:36.810
Maybe a separate entity is
causing the fire in the firewood.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:40.450
And maybe the firewood has
nothing to do with the fire.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.200
And maybe the mantra has nothing to do

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.563
with curing the cancer.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:51.273
Maybe they're both coming
from somewhere else.

00:20:51.273 --> 00:20:53.130
RTAG TU 'BAR BA NYID DU 'GYUR

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:56.114
Then not only would your
toilet break out on in fire,

00:20:56.114 --> 00:20:56.947
but RTAG TU

00:20:56.947 --> 00:21:01.720
means it would never go out,
because there's no wood.

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.443
It just burns by itself.

00:21:05.022 --> 00:21:07.580
'BAR BYED RGYU LAS MI 'BYUNG ZHING

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:12.580
Furthermore, you could have
fires without any fuel.

00:21:15.651 --> 00:21:17.480
RTZOM PA DON MED NYID DU 'GYUR

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.540
And you wouldn't have
to go through the effort

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.950
of collecting firewood
because you could have a fire

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:22.783
without the firewood.

00:21:22.783 --> 00:21:25.010
So why go through all the
trouble of finding firewood

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:29.740
or buying oil for your
car, gasoline for your car?

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.820
Because it's going to
burn without the gasoline.

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:35.553
The engine is going to
burn without the gasoline.

00:21:35.553 --> 00:21:39.560
Then he gives another
verse. And I was confused

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.680
when I first read it

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:43.050
because it seems like he
repeats the same thing.

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:46.100
But I tell you, if you
look at it carefully,

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.790
you will see that verse three

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:50.277
is a justification of verse two.

00:21:50.277 --> 00:21:53.272
And you can cook that
and you can work on that.

00:21:53.272 --> 00:21:54.992
GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA'I PHYIR

00:21:54.992 --> 00:21:59.450
If the fire didn't depend on the wood,

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:01.930
then yes, fires could break out everywhere

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:04.063
and they would go forever.

00:22:04.063 --> 00:22:07.530
'BAR BAR BYED RGYU LAS MI 'BYUNG

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.650
And the fires would go for always

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.083
because they didn't have to have fuel.

00:22:14.431 --> 00:22:16.100
RTAG TU 'BAR BA YIN NA NI

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:18.887
They will also burn forever
because they didn't have fuel,

00:22:18.887 --> 00:22:21.329
and the fuel can't run out.

00:22:21.329 --> 00:22:24.810
RTZOM PA DON MED NYID DU 'GYUR

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:27.010
And you wouldn't have
to go collect firewood

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:30.993
or buy gasoline for your engine to run.

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:34.080
And that's similar to the assertion

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:37.980
that the eye wouldn't have to depend,

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:41.813
the eyeball wouldn't have
to depend on its causes,

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:44.900
because it had no connection to them.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:48.960
And it wouldn't be the cause of seeing.

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:52.030
Because the seeing and the eyeball

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.550
and the chemicals in the eye were separate

00:22:54.550 --> 00:22:56.330
and never overlapped.

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:57.320
You've got to think about it.

00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:59.110
He's really making the same argument

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:02.450
that he made in the last
chapter, which is the point

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:04.500
because this chapter is
used by the other guy

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:07.060
to prove his points in the last chapter.

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:09.480
So don't forget when we're
talking about fire and firewood,

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:11.210
we're really talking about the eye,

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:14.350
the astronomer, and the stars.

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:17.760
All right... And the sun
would really burn forever.

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:19.183
Here's the sun.

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:25.360
If the fuel, the hydrogen,
that makes the sun burn,

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:28.030
and the sun were separate,

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:29.660
then the sun would never burn out,

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:31.283
because it has no fuel.

00:23:32.774 --> 00:23:35.470
You would just have this
fire going on forever.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:37.520
And this sun would never burn out.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.670
The Abhidharma says our
sun is going to burn out.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:43.870
And Stephen Hawkins says the same thing.

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:46.970
So probably he was an
Abhidharma guy, I don't know.

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:49.233
All right, next verse.

00:23:54.416 --> 00:23:56.766
,DE LA GAL TE 'DI SNYAM DU,

00:23:56.766 --> 00:23:58.724
,SREG BZHIN BUD SHING YIN SEMS NA,

00:23:58.724 --> 00:24:01.048
,GANG TSE DE TZAM DE YIN NA,

00:24:01.048 --> 00:24:03.920
,GANG GIS BUD SHING DE SREG BYED,

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:07.670
And by the way, this is
a... what do you call it?

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.880
This is a method employed
by Nagarjuna again:

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:21.410
he will disprove something
that somebody else said,

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:25.260
then he kind of gives the other
guy a chance to come back,

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:27.160
and then he smashes him.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:30.090
So he punches him with the first verse.

00:24:30.090 --> 00:24:33.180
The guy comes back. And then
the Nagarjuna knocks him out

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:35.363
with the second verse. So it's called

00:24:35.363 --> 00:24:37.130
MA NGES PA SPANG BA

00:24:37.130 --> 00:24:40.520
It means Nagarjuna is nailing it down.

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:43.710
So then this verse is kind of
the same as the last verse,

00:24:43.710 --> 00:24:46.810
but it's meant to knock
the guy out forever.

00:24:46.810 --> 00:24:49.810
The first one just
punched him. Here we go.

00:24:51.255 --> 00:24:54.008
DE LA GAL TE 'DI SNYAM DU

00:24:54.008 --> 00:24:55.390
And now suppose you think to yourself,

00:24:55.390 --> 00:24:57.368
he says to the other guy,

00:24:57.368 --> 00:24:59.750
SREG BZHIN BUD SHING YIN SEMS NA

00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:01.540
the burning is the wood.

00:25:04.090 --> 00:25:07.200
Don't forget we had fire, agni.

00:25:07.200 --> 00:25:09.130
We had firewood, indhana.

00:25:12.600 --> 00:25:15.820
We had burning, daha.

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:18.653
And then this guy... now the
guy says, "You know what?

00:25:20.490 --> 00:25:23.860
The burning is the wood."

00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:25.950
The burning is wood.

00:25:25.950 --> 00:25:27.070
They are not separate.

00:25:27.070 --> 00:25:32.070
And frankly, his example
of a fire is controversial.

00:25:33.590 --> 00:25:35.710
It's difficult to thresh
it out in our own mind

00:25:35.710 --> 00:25:39.790
because really when a piece
of wood is really burning,

00:25:39.790 --> 00:25:42.390
it's kind of hard to distinguish
between where the fire ends

00:25:42.390 --> 00:25:45.876
and where the wood starts.

00:25:45.876 --> 00:25:48.209
,`GANG TSE DE TZAM DE YIN NA,

00:25:48.209 --> 00:25:51.700
,GANG GIS BUD SHING DE SREG BYED,

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:55.470
If the burning is the firewood
then what burns the firewood,

00:25:55.470 --> 00:25:56.303
except for the firewood?

00:25:56.303 --> 00:25:58.103
Does the firewood burn the firewood?

00:25:59.200 --> 00:26:00.820
That's Nagarjuna.

00:26:00.820 --> 00:26:02.450
I'll say it again.

00:26:02.450 --> 00:26:03.836
That guy says, "You know what?

00:26:03.836 --> 00:26:04.861
"If you really thinks about it,

00:26:04.861 --> 00:26:07.670
"the fire and the firewood
are kind of mixed up."

00:26:07.670 --> 00:26:09.627
And then Nagarjuna says, "Yeah, cool.

00:26:09.627 --> 00:26:10.817
"So the firewood burns the firewood,

00:26:10.817 --> 00:26:13.298
"and you don't need the fire.

00:26:14.757 --> 00:26:17.270
"Because the firewood is the burning."

00:26:17.270 --> 00:26:19.407
He said, "The burning and the firewood

00:26:19.407 --> 00:26:20.850
"are kind of mixed up."

00:26:20.850 --> 00:26:22.637
So Nagarjuna said, "Yeah, that's fine.

00:26:22.637 --> 00:26:24.307
"So just put a couple of sticks together,

00:26:24.307 --> 00:26:27.847
"and they can burn each
other without fire,

00:26:27.847 --> 00:26:29.737
"because the one stick is already mixed up

00:26:29.737 --> 00:26:31.619
"with the fire."

00:26:31.619 --> 00:26:33.220
Like that.

00:26:33.220 --> 00:26:35.547
All right, the burning of the
wood couldn't burn the wood.

00:26:35.547 --> 00:26:38.410
What's the picture, Pachi?

00:26:38.410 --> 00:26:41.510
Oh, that's why the boy
is looking confused.

00:26:41.510 --> 00:26:43.143
He just heard this verse.

00:26:45.119 --> 00:26:46.180
[Geshe Michael chuckles]

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:47.953
If the burning was the fire...

00:26:49.729 --> 00:26:51.227
if the burning was the firewood,

00:26:51.227 --> 00:26:53.810
then, one match could burn another match

00:26:53.810 --> 00:26:57.050
without a fire, got it?

00:26:57.050 --> 00:26:58.870
That's why the boy is looking confused.

00:26:58.870 --> 00:27:01.663
All right, this boy represents you guys.

00:27:02.586 --> 00:27:04.360
[Geshe Michael laughs]

00:27:04.360 --> 00:27:05.193
Next verse.

00:27:05.193 --> 00:27:07.740
- And what's it got to do with mantra?

00:27:07.740 --> 00:27:11.280
- Oh, saying the Mantra
is curing the cancer.

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:16.280
- Okay, so then curing the cancer

00:27:18.866 --> 00:27:20.710
is caused by curing the cancer,

00:27:20.710 --> 00:27:22.577
and you don't have to do a mantra.

00:27:22.577 --> 00:27:25.160
Because curing the cancer is the mantra.

00:27:25.160 --> 00:27:27.090
The mantra is curing the cancer.

00:27:27.090 --> 00:27:29.220
The mantra cures the cancer.

00:27:29.220 --> 00:27:32.130
The mantra is curing the cancer.

00:27:32.130 --> 00:27:34.410
- Okay, so curing the
cancer is curing the cancer,

00:27:34.410 --> 00:27:38.560
and you don't need a
mantra, you can just relax.

00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:39.770
Okay, got it?

00:27:41.860 --> 00:27:46.140
The mantra is curing the cancer.

00:27:46.140 --> 00:27:47.300
- Okay.

00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:49.020
- Then you don't need a mantra.

00:27:49.020 --> 00:27:50.060
- Why?

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:52.200
- Because curing the
cancer can cure the cancer.

00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:53.120
- Why?

00:27:53.120 --> 00:27:57.160
- Because the mantra is curing the cancer.

00:27:57.160 --> 00:27:58.660
Okay, got it?

00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:04.550
All right. By the way, if
you don't think about it

00:28:04.550 --> 00:28:06.220
and you just give up,

00:28:06.220 --> 00:28:08.450
you won't be able to use mantras.

00:28:08.450 --> 00:28:11.040
So I'm sorry, you have to
think about this stuff.

00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:13.893
You have to go into retreat
at Diamond Mountain,

00:28:14.790 --> 00:28:17.603
in your spare time think about this thing.

00:28:18.617 --> 00:28:19.720
And then you'll figure it out.

00:28:19.720 --> 00:28:20.910
One day you'll figure it out.

00:28:20.910 --> 00:28:22.720
And then the mantra will work,

00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:25.700
qhich is exciting

00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:29.660
And by the way, I mean,
it's going to take time.

00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:31.420
- Oh Geshe-la, should I stop my mantras

00:28:31.420 --> 00:28:33.200
until I can understand Nagarjuna?

00:28:33.200 --> 00:28:34.630
- I didn't say that.

00:28:34.630 --> 00:28:35.550
Keep doing the mantras,

00:28:35.550 --> 00:28:37.530
they're going to help
you understand Nagarjuna.

00:28:37.530 --> 00:28:38.810
And then understanding Nagarjuna

00:28:38.810 --> 00:28:40.460
will have the mantras work.

00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:44.546
Verse five I think.

00:28:44.546 --> 00:28:46.471
,GZHAN PHYIR MI PHRAD PHRAD MED NA,

00:28:46.471 --> 00:28:48.787
,SREG PAR MI 'GYUR MI SREG NA,

00:28:48.787 --> 00:28:51.420
,'CHI BAR MI 'GYUR MI 'CHI NA,

00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:53.869
,RANG RTAGS DANG YANG LDAN PAR GNAS,

00:28:56.283 --> 00:28:59.460
GZHAN PHYIR MI PHRAD

00:28:59.460 --> 00:29:04.320
- Okay, does the fire...
is the fire the firewood?

00:29:04.320 --> 00:29:05.680
- We already said no.

00:29:05.680 --> 00:29:08.890
- Okay, so the fire and the
firewood is separate, right?

00:29:08.890 --> 00:29:10.500
- Yeah, they're separate.

00:29:10.500 --> 00:29:12.660
- Okay, and they can't overlap, right?

00:29:12.660 --> 00:29:14.130
- Right, they cannot overlap.

00:29:14.130 --> 00:29:14.963
- Why?

00:29:14.963 --> 00:29:18.060
- There cannot be an inch of
the fire which is the firewood.

00:29:18.060 --> 00:29:19.010
Either all the fire is the firewood

00:29:19.010 --> 00:29:21.440
or the fire is not the firewood.

00:29:21.440 --> 00:29:22.800
They've got to be separate.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:23.640
- Are they separate?

00:29:23.640 --> 00:29:24.530
- Yes.

00:29:24.530 --> 00:29:25.710
- Do they ever overlap?

00:29:25.710 --> 00:29:27.290
- No.

00:29:27.290 --> 00:29:31.610
- Okay, so then the fire
can't burn the wood.

00:29:31.610 --> 00:29:32.443
- Why?

00:29:32.443 --> 00:29:34.398
- It never touches the wood.

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:38.610
- No, they do touch.

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:39.970
- Okay, then they overlap.

00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:41.920
- Okay. Then the firewood is the fire.

00:29:41.920 --> 00:29:42.753
- Right.

00:29:42.753 --> 00:29:43.657
- Then the firewood can burn the firewood,

00:29:43.657 --> 00:29:46.580
and you don't need a match?

00:29:47.610 --> 00:29:48.530
It's true.

00:29:48.530 --> 00:29:50.700
It doesn't make sense, there's
something weird going on.

00:29:50.700 --> 00:29:52.610
You just never thought about it.

00:29:52.610 --> 00:29:54.260
Don't blame Nagarjuna.

00:29:57.029 --> 00:29:59.330
The things you used to
think were causing things,

00:29:59.330 --> 00:30:02.520
aren't causing things, but you
spend your whole life lazy,

00:30:02.520 --> 00:30:04.050
not thinking about it.

00:30:04.050 --> 00:30:05.710
And you keep taking aspirin,

00:30:05.710 --> 00:30:09.270
even though it doesn't work half the time.

00:30:09.270 --> 00:30:11.950
All right. And you keep doing mantras,

00:30:11.950 --> 00:30:13.909
even though they don't work half the time.

00:30:13.909 --> 00:30:15.450
GZHAN PHYIR MI PHRAD PHRAD MED NA

00:30:15.450 --> 00:30:18.067
If the fire never touches the firewood

00:30:18.067 --> 00:30:19.223
and they never overlap,

00:30:20.203 --> 00:30:21.360
SREG PAR MI 'GYUR

00:30:21.360 --> 00:30:23.750
there cannot be a burning.

00:30:23.750 --> 00:30:28.750
If the fire, if the agni
never touches the indhana

00:30:29.032 --> 00:30:32.770
Right? There cannot be a daha.

00:30:32.770 --> 00:30:36.500
If the agni never touches the indhana,

00:30:36.500 --> 00:30:39.730
then there can never be a daha.

00:30:39.730 --> 00:30:44.300
If the fire never touches the firewood,

00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:47.330
then there cannot be a burning.

00:30:47.330 --> 00:30:51.120
And if there's no burning,
there's no nirvana.

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:53.037
What does that mean?

00:30:53.951 --> 00:30:56.090
[indistinct Chattering]

00:30:56.090 --> 00:31:01.090
If there's no fire, then there's
no fire going out, nirvana.

00:31:01.830 --> 00:31:03.880
And this is where the word nirvana comes.

00:31:03.880 --> 00:31:07.697
If there's no fire, if
the firewood never...

00:31:07.697 --> 00:31:11.270
if the fire never touches the firewood,

00:31:11.270 --> 00:31:14.410
then there's not going to be any fire.

00:31:14.410 --> 00:31:16.870
And if there's no fire to start,

00:31:16.870 --> 00:31:20.283
then the fire is never
going to stop. Nirvana.

00:31:21.160 --> 00:31:24.090
Then if it never stops, MI 'CHI NA

00:31:24.090 --> 00:31:28.470
MI 'CHI NA, which in the
Sanskrit is anirvāṇa (anirvana).

00:31:29.470 --> 00:31:31.403
If there's no stopping of the fire,

00:31:32.301 --> 00:31:36.051
RANG RTAGS DANG YANG LDAN PAR GNAS

00:31:38.460 --> 00:31:40.190
then the fire is going to be hot forever

00:31:40.190 --> 00:31:43.090
because burning is part of the fire

00:31:43.090 --> 00:31:45.900
and it can never go out
and it can never start.

00:31:45.900 --> 00:31:48.650
So every time something is a fire

00:31:48.650 --> 00:31:50.060
it's going to burn forever.

00:31:50.060 --> 00:31:52.380
It's just going to burn.

00:31:52.380 --> 00:31:54.763
It will never lose its

00:31:56.088 --> 00:31:57.200
svalinga

00:31:57.200 --> 00:32:00.590
in Sanskrit, "linga" means its sign.

00:32:00.590 --> 00:32:04.220
By the way, which means a
male sign and a female sign.

00:32:04.220 --> 00:32:07.853
But in philosophy it means

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:12.020
the fire would never
lose his hot and burning.

00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:14.016
And it would burn forever.

00:32:14.016 --> 00:32:15.180
svalinga

00:32:15.180 --> 00:32:18.240
It would keep it's own sign forever.

00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:19.220
- Why?

00:32:19.220 --> 00:32:20.820
- Because it never went out.

00:32:20.820 --> 00:32:21.700
- Why?

00:32:21.700 --> 00:32:23.210
- Because it never burned.

00:32:23.210 --> 00:32:24.043
- Why?

00:32:24.043 --> 00:32:26.530
- Because the fire never
touched the firewood.

00:32:27.747 --> 00:32:29.443
Something you've got to cook.

00:32:30.460 --> 00:32:33.710
All right, we did the
Sanskrit part already,

00:32:33.710 --> 00:32:38.710
let's go... Yeah, and by the way,

00:32:38.710 --> 00:32:39.997
Nagarjuna wraps it up and says,

00:32:39.997 --> 00:32:42.690
"By the way, if the fire
could burn the firewood

00:32:42.690 --> 00:32:46.134
without any contact, then you could...",

00:32:46.134 --> 00:32:49.884
next picture Pachi? Tim?

00:32:52.440 --> 00:32:54.130
"...then a match will light a cigarette

00:32:54.130 --> 00:32:56.330
without ever touching the cigarette."

00:32:56.330 --> 00:32:58.020
The fire doesn't have
to touch the cigarette.

00:32:58.020 --> 00:33:01.030
If a fire could happen without overlapping

00:33:01.030 --> 00:33:03.100
between the fire and the firewood,

00:33:03.100 --> 00:33:08.100
then somebody could start
a lighter in Guadalajara

00:33:09.410 --> 00:33:12.820
and the cigarette will burn in Sedona.

00:33:12.820 --> 00:33:15.620
Because they don't have to
touch, according to you.

00:33:16.830 --> 00:33:19.330
All right, we don't want to smoke anyway.

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:21.330
I felt weird about it.

00:33:21.330 --> 00:33:25.210
Next two verses, six and seven.

00:33:25.210 --> 00:33:29.340
Now, this is one of those
tricky spots in Nagarjuna.

00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:31.570
Verse six is the other guy

00:33:31.570 --> 00:33:33.415
and verse seven is Nagarjuna.

00:33:33.415 --> 00:33:35.720
But he doesn't tell you.

00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:40.370
Now when you get really
good at reading scripture,

00:33:40.370 --> 00:33:43.930
you know which verse is fake
and which verse is right.

00:33:43.930 --> 00:33:47.110
But if you don't, you better
get a good commentary.

00:33:47.110 --> 00:33:50.870
I've heard many people explain
the other guy's position

00:33:50.870 --> 00:33:54.410
as Nagarjuna's position, very eloquently.

00:33:54.410 --> 00:33:56.650
And it's just totally wrong.

00:33:56.650 --> 00:33:58.860
By the way, in my opinion,

00:33:58.860 --> 00:34:02.360
I'm not aware of any good
translation of the root text,

00:34:02.360 --> 00:34:05.533
I don't think so. Correct
one - I don't think so.

00:34:06.831 --> 00:34:08.414
,JI LTAR BUD MED SKYES PA DANG,

00:34:08.414 --> 00:34:10.681
,SKYES PA'ANG BUD MED PHRAD PA BZHIN,

00:34:10.681 --> 00:34:13.146
,GAL TE SHING LAS ME GZHAN NA,

00:34:13.146 --> 00:34:15.405
,SHING DANG PHRAD DU RUNG BAR 'GYUR,

00:34:16.520 --> 00:34:17.417
The other guy says,

00:34:17.417 --> 00:34:20.287
"Look, when a man touches a woman

00:34:20.287 --> 00:34:23.920
"and a woman touches a
man, they're different."

00:34:23.920 --> 00:34:25.051
What is the -

00:34:25.051 --> 00:34:26.884
Vive la différence -

00:34:26.884 --> 00:34:28.543
A woman is not a man,
and a man is not a woman.

00:34:30.150 --> 00:34:32.160
And that's the only reason they can touch.

00:34:32.160 --> 00:34:35.960
If they were the same thing,
then they would never touch.

00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:38.080
And then we wouldn't be here
because our mom and our dad

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:40.120
would not have touched each other, right?

00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:41.897
So he says,

00:34:41.897 --> 00:34:46.897
"Look, women touch men
and men touch women.

00:34:46.977 --> 00:34:51.977
"And it's only if the firewood
and the fire are separate

00:34:52.677 --> 00:34:56.150
"that you could have
touching between them."

00:34:56.150 --> 00:34:58.583
Things can't touch if
they're not different.

00:34:59.460 --> 00:35:02.210
A thing doesn't touch
itself. You see what I mean?

00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:05.800
A coffee cup can't touch a coffee cup.

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:08.950
This coffee cup doesn't
touch this coffee cup

00:35:08.950 --> 00:35:11.060
because it's not different
from this coffee cup.

00:35:11.060 --> 00:35:14.570
This coffee cup is not
different from this coffee cup,

00:35:14.570 --> 00:35:16.160
so they could never make contact

00:35:16.160 --> 00:35:17.950
because they're the same thing.

00:35:17.950 --> 00:35:20.940
To have contact, things
have to be different.

00:35:20.940 --> 00:35:23.370
And then they can contact each other.

00:35:23.370 --> 00:35:25.460
Therefore, come on, it's simple.

00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:27.770
It's like boys and girls.

00:35:27.770 --> 00:35:30.270
And then they touch, they're different.

00:35:30.270 --> 00:35:31.840
So the fire and the firewood,

00:35:31.840 --> 00:35:33.610
they have to be different things.

00:35:33.610 --> 00:35:34.602
The other guy says,

00:35:34.602 --> 00:35:36.830
"I don't know why you're
getting it so complicated."

00:35:36.830 --> 00:35:40.580
That's verse number six, am I right? Yeah.

00:35:40.580 --> 00:35:43.760
Now, verse number seven is our answer.

00:35:43.760 --> 00:35:45.418
Nagarjuna's answer.

00:35:45.418 --> 00:35:47.018
,GAL TE ME DANG SHING DAG NI,

00:35:47.018 --> 00:35:48.651
,GCIG GIS GCIG NI BSAL GYUR NA,

00:35:49.709 --> 00:35:52.792
,SHING LAS ME GZHAN NYID YIN YANG,

00:35:52.792 --> 00:35:55.249
,SHING DANG PHRAD PAR 'DOD LA RAG,

00:35:55.249 --> 00:35:59.450
Now we go back to that verb we had

00:35:59.450 --> 00:36:01.940
where one thing illuminates another thing,

00:36:01.940 --> 00:36:05.830
or one thing delineates another thing.

00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:07.731
And he says, you know what?

00:36:07.731 --> 00:36:09.639
,GAL TE ME DANG SHING DAG NI,

00:36:09.639 --> 00:36:12.547
,GCIG GIS GCIG NI BSAL GYUR

00:36:12.547 --> 00:36:17.500
"Is it that juice bottles
define coffee cups,

00:36:18.660 --> 00:36:21.240
and coffee cups define juice bottles?"

00:36:21.240 --> 00:36:26.240
Is it that women define
men, and men define women?

00:36:26.330 --> 00:36:28.793
In that case, they have
to be separate, right?

00:36:32.090 --> 00:36:35.630
If they "touch"... By the way,

00:36:35.630 --> 00:36:37.800
the other guy was talking about touching

00:36:37.800 --> 00:36:40.850
in the sense of physically
touching each other,

00:36:40.850 --> 00:36:43.970
but Nagarjuna takes it to, "Okay.

00:36:43.970 --> 00:36:48.970
So, you can't really tell a man is a man

00:36:49.350 --> 00:36:53.650
until he's in a room with a woman."

00:36:53.650 --> 00:36:58.650
You can't distinguish male without female.

00:36:59.910 --> 00:37:02.240
In that sense, they have to touch,

00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:03.790
meaning they have to
be in the same picture.

00:37:03.790 --> 00:37:06.883
We've got a picture here, I think so.

00:37:09.410 --> 00:37:13.540
Male and female have
to be in the same photo

00:37:13.540 --> 00:37:15.830
to appreciate the difference

00:37:15.830 --> 00:37:17.540
between a man and a woman.

00:37:17.540 --> 00:37:19.690
They have to be in the same photo.

00:37:19.690 --> 00:37:21.700
And then you can say, oh,
look, he's got a beard,

00:37:21.700 --> 00:37:23.110
she doesn't have a beard.

00:37:23.110 --> 00:37:25.926
She's got lipstick, he doesn't have that.

00:37:25.926 --> 00:37:27.189
I don't know exactly, but...

00:37:27.189 --> 00:37:30.220
So when they're in the same photo,

00:37:30.220 --> 00:37:33.340
when the juice bottle is
next to the coffee cup,

00:37:33.340 --> 00:37:38.120
then you can tell the
contrast defines each one.

00:37:38.120 --> 00:37:40.090
Each one defines the other.

00:37:40.090 --> 00:37:43.930
When you put them in the
same frame of your camera,

00:37:43.930 --> 00:37:46.030
your video right now.

00:37:46.030 --> 00:37:47.300
When you put them in the same frame,

00:37:47.300 --> 00:37:50.430
then this one speaks to the
difference between that one,

00:37:50.430 --> 00:37:53.605
and this one speaks to the
difference from that one.

00:37:53.605 --> 00:37:54.438
,GAL TE ME DANG SHING DAG NI,

00:37:54.438 --> 00:37:56.510
,GCIG GIS GCIG NI BSAL GYUR NA,

00:37:56.510 --> 00:37:58.180
Are you saying they define each other?

00:37:58.180 --> 00:37:59.536
Yes, okay.

00:37:59.536 --> 00:38:00.369
,SHING LAS ME GZHAN NYID YIN YANG,

00:38:00.369 --> 00:38:03.720
,SHING DANG PHRAD PAR 'DOD LA RAG,

00:38:03.720 --> 00:38:05.620
Then you have to say they make contact.

00:38:06.932 --> 00:38:08.480
'DOD -  'DOD PA

00:38:08.480 --> 00:38:10.090
You have to be believe they make contact.

00:38:10.090 --> 00:38:11.710
- Do they make contact?

00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:12.543
- Yes.

00:38:12.543 --> 00:38:13.376
- Do they overlap?

00:38:13.376 --> 00:38:14.209
- No.

00:38:14.209 --> 00:38:15.770
- Do they make contact
without overlapping?

00:38:15.770 --> 00:38:16.603
- Yes.

00:38:16.603 --> 00:38:17.553
- Where's the point of contact?

00:38:17.553 --> 00:38:19.061
- It's where they overlap.

00:38:20.967 --> 00:38:22.160
[Geshe Michael chuckles]

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:25.800
- So don't tell me that
males define females

00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:29.020
and females define males,
because they can't touch.

00:38:29.020 --> 00:38:31.230
- No, they have to touch
to define each other.

00:38:31.230 --> 00:38:33.160
- That's correct, so they have to overlap.

00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:35.530
- No Geshe-la, they touch
without overlapping.

00:38:35.530 --> 00:38:37.520
- Okay, so there's no point
where they touch, right?

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:40.910
There's no point where
one overlaps the same area

00:38:40.910 --> 00:38:43.200
with the other, which
is what contact means.

00:38:43.200 --> 00:38:44.490
Get used to that.

00:38:44.490 --> 00:38:48.570
It's not that there's a tiny
tip of the male that...well...

00:38:48.570 --> 00:38:52.263
It's not that there's a
tiny tip of the bottle

00:38:52.263 --> 00:38:55.250
that touches a tiny tip of the coffee cup.

00:38:55.250 --> 00:38:57.548
At some point they have to overlap.

00:38:57.548 --> 00:39:02.378
Or else they don't touch, and
then they are disconnected.

00:39:02.378 --> 00:39:04.723
And you can't say one
is defined by the other.

00:39:05.640 --> 00:39:07.292
You can't say one is delineated,

00:39:07.292 --> 00:39:08.907
@adhyate,

00:39:08.907 --> 00:39:10.610
by the other, you can't say that.

00:39:10.610 --> 00:39:12.620
It's very subtle, and
if you think about it,

00:39:12.620 --> 00:39:13.890
you'll get it.

00:39:13.890 --> 00:39:16.650
Don't give up, don't be lazy.

00:39:16.650 --> 00:39:18.820
You want to cure
someone's cancer with your

00:39:18.820 --> 00:39:21.570
Medicine Buddha mantras?
You've got to figure this out.

00:39:21.570 --> 00:39:24.890
And I say, if you don't understand this,

00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:28.100
you cannot cure another
person with your mantras

00:39:28.100 --> 00:39:30.510
because then you don't
know what you're doing.

00:39:30.510 --> 00:39:33.590
Then you're yelling at the
husband who's not in the kitchen.

00:39:33.590 --> 00:39:37.130
Doing mantras, without
understanding them, to cure cancer

00:39:37.130 --> 00:39:39.270
is like yelling at the
husband in the kitchen

00:39:39.270 --> 00:39:41.680
who's not there.

00:39:41.680 --> 00:39:44.080
It's a same thing.

00:39:44.080 --> 00:39:47.430
Woah! Okay, yeah, we've got that one.

00:39:51.780 --> 00:39:54.427
Hey, we finished the class! Yay!

00:39:54.427 --> 00:39:58.640
So think about it.

00:39:58.640 --> 00:40:01.040
Can they touch without overlapping?

00:40:01.040 --> 00:40:01.873
No.

00:40:03.498 --> 00:40:06.050
Well, if they overlap,
then they don't touch,

00:40:06.050 --> 00:40:07.313
then they're the same thing.

00:40:07.313 --> 00:40:08.887
Then the man is the woman,

00:40:08.887 --> 00:40:12.260
and a little part of him is the woman.

00:40:12.260 --> 00:40:15.670
And they don't define each other.

00:40:15.670 --> 00:40:20.670
And the point is, for us, a
mantra cannot cure cancer,

00:40:21.410 --> 00:40:23.790
if the mantra doesn't touch the cancer

00:40:23.790 --> 00:40:26.293
and the mantra cannot touch the cancer.

00:40:27.790 --> 00:40:30.570
- So Geshe-la, why the
heck should I do mantras?

00:40:30.570 --> 00:40:34.050
- Because there's one
thing causing the mantra,

00:40:34.050 --> 00:40:37.210
which also causes the curing.

00:40:37.210 --> 00:40:38.950
- Well, what's that?

00:40:38.950 --> 00:40:43.250
- That's saving life of animals.

00:40:43.250 --> 00:40:44.790
Saving the life of the animals

00:40:44.790 --> 00:40:49.383
makes the mantra work to cure
cancer. Think about that.

00:40:50.270 --> 00:40:52.623
All right, see you guys
in the next class, yay!

